{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>In all the way.</b> Meaning right and left. And this commandment and the statutes and the judgments, their essence is \"that you may fear,\" you and your son and your son's son. And behold, the essence of all the commandments is faith of the heart. And when you fear HaShem, this is the whole person. And on account of this the human being was created, as the words of Ecclesiastes. And furthermore, they will prolong days — with the collective, upon the earth; and with the individual, in the world to come (variant: this one)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "I read ״עם הכל״ as ״with the collective,״ parallel to ״היחיד״ (the individual); the parenthetical ס״א הזה (variant: this one) appears to offer an alternate reading for ״העולם הבא״."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:31.931460381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}